{"title": "<span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Heating curve of water</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的加热曲线</span>", "slides": [{"id": "c5-heating-curve:title", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker\">🌡️ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Phase Changes &amp; Energy</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">相变与能量</span></div><h2 class=\"s-title\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Heating curve of water</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的加热曲线</span></h2><p class=\"s-hook\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The burner under a pot of ice water is on full, yet the thermometer is stuck at 0 °C for minutes — where is all that heat going?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">一锅冰水下面的火开到最大，温度计却好几分钟都停在 0 °C——那么多热量跑到哪里去了？</span></span></p><div class=\"s-diff\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Difficulty</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">难度</span> <b>●●○</b></div><div class=\"s-meta\">⏱ 35 min · ★ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">essential</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">必会</span></div>"}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve:keys", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker\">🔑 <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Must know</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">必须记住</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Heating curve of water</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的加热曲线</span></div><ol class=\"s-list\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Diagonal = temperature changing (one phase). Horizontal = phase changing (two phases), T constant.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">斜线＝温度变（一个相）。水平线＝相变（两个相），温度不变。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Water: 1 ice warms · 2 melts at 0 °C · 3 liquid warms · 4 boils at 100 °C · 5 steam warms.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水：1 冰升温 · 2 0 °C 熔化 · 3 液体升温 · 4 100 °C 沸腾 · 5 水蒸气升温。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Flat because energy breaks attractions or separates particles, not speeding them up.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">平台是因为能量用来打破吸引或分开粒子，而不是让粒子加速。</span></div></li></ol><div class=\"s-formula\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">diagonal</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">\u21d2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">temperature\u00a0changes</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:1em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">horizontal</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">\u21d2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">phase\u00a0changes</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div class=\"s-fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 420 260\" class=\"fig wide\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"heating curve of water\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"212.8\" x2=\"408\" y2=\"212.8\" class=\"g\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"216.8\" text-anchor=\"end\" class=\"lbl s\">-20°C</text><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"186.2\" x2=\"408\" y2=\"186.2\" class=\"g\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"190.2\" text-anchor=\"end\" class=\"lbl s\">0°C</text><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"53.8\" x2=\"408\" y2=\"53.8\" class=\"g\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"57.8\" text-anchor=\"end\" class=\"lbl s\">100°C</text><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"27.2\" x2=\"408\" y2=\"27.2\" class=\"g\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"31.2\" text-anchor=\"end\" class=\"lbl s\">120°C</text><line x1=\"54\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"54\" y2=\"226\" class=\"ax\"/><line x1=\"54\" y1=\"226\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"226\" class=\"ax\"/><polyline points=\"54.0,212.8 96.1,186.2 180.4,186.2 222.6,53.8 357.4,53.8 399.6,27.2\" class=\"curve\"/><circle cx=\"75.1\" cy=\"199.5\" r=\"11\" class=\"hcn\"/><text x=\"75.1\" y=\"203.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"hct\">1</text><text x=\"91.1\" y=\"217.5\" class=\"lbl s\"><tspan class=\"en\">solid</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 固</tspan></text><circle cx=\"138.3\" cy=\"186.2\" r=\"11\" class=\"hcn\"/><text x=\"138.3\" y=\"190.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"hct\">2</text><text x=\"138.3\" y=\"170.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s\"><tspan class=\"en\">melting</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 熔化</tspan></text><circle cx=\"201.5\" cy=\"120.0\" r=\"11\" class=\"hcn\"/><text x=\"201.5\" y=\"124.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"hct\">3</text><text x=\"217.5\" y=\"138.0\" class=\"lbl s\"><tspan class=\"en\">liquid</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 液</tspan></text><circle cx=\"290.0\" cy=\"53.8\" r=\"11\" class=\"hcn\"/><text x=\"290.0\" y=\"57.8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"hct\">4</text><text x=\"290.0\" y=\"37.8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s\"><tspan class=\"en\">boiling</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 沸腾</tspan></text><circle cx=\"378.5\" cy=\"40.5\" r=\"11\" class=\"hcn\"/><text x=\"378.5\" y=\"44.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"hct\">5</text><text x=\"394.5\" y=\"58.5\" class=\"lbl s\"><tspan class=\"en\">gas</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 气</tspan></text><text x=\"237.0\" y=\"252\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s\"><tspan class=\"en\">Heat added (time) →</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 吸收的热量（时间）→</tspan></text><text x=\"14\" y=\"130.0\" transform=\"rotate(-90 14 130.0)\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s\"><tspan class=\"en\">Temperature</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 温度</tspan></text></svg></div>"}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve:hard", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker hard\">🧗 <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The hard part</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">难点</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Heating curve of water</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的加热曲线</span></div><h3 class=\"s-h\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Why the temperature stops rising</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">为什么温度不再上升</span></span></h3><p class=\"s-why\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">It feels wrong that adding heat does not raise the temperature.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">「加热却不升温」违反直觉。</span></span></p><ol class=\"s-steps\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Temperature tracks how fast particles move.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">温度反映粒子运动的快慢。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">On a flat part, energy goes into pulling particles apart.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水平段上，能量用来把粒子拉开。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Speed unchanged → temperature unchanged until the phase change is complete.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">速度不变 → 温度不变，直到相变完成。</span></div></li></ol><div class=\"s-try\"><b><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Try</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">试一试</span></b> <div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Ice at −20 °C is heated to 120 °C. How many flat segments?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">−20 °C 的冰加热到 120 °C，有几个水平段？</span></div><details><summary><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Answer</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">答案</span></summary><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">2 (melting at 0 °C, boiling at 100 °C).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">2 个（0 °C 熔化，100 °C 沸腾）。</span></div></details></div>"}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve:traps", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker trap\">⚠️ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Traps &amp; tip</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">陷阱与提示</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Heating curve of water</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的加热曲线</span></div><ul class=\"s-list traps\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Heat added → temperature must rise ✗ → not on the flat parts ✓</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">加热 → 温度一定升 ✗ → 水平段上不升 ✓</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Flat part = one phase ✗ → two phases together ✓</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水平段＝一个相 ✗ → 两个相共存 ✓</span></div></li></ul><div class=\"s-tnote\">🟡 <div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Your class notes put \"heat added\" on the x-axis. Many textbooks put \"time\" there instead (with heat added at a steady rate) — the shape and the five segments are exactly the same, so read either graph the same way.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">课堂笔记的横轴是「加入的热量」。很多教科书横轴写的是「时间」（假设匀速加热）——曲线形状和五段完全一样，两种图读法相同。</span></div></div><div class=\"s-tip\">🎯 <div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Cooling curve = read right to left: condense at 100 °C, freeze at 0 °C.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">冷却曲线＝从右往左读：100 °C 液化，0 °C 凝固。</span></div></div>"}], "cards": [{"id": "c5-heating-curve.c0", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Diagonal line on a heating curve?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">加热曲线上的斜线？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Temperature is changing (one phase warming).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">温度在变（单一相在升温）。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.c1", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Horizontal line?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水平线？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Phase is changing; temperature constant; two phases present.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">相在变；温度不变；两个相共存。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.c2", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Water: melting and boiling temperatures?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的熔点和沸点？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">0 °C and 100 °C.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">0 °C 和 100 °C。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.c3", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Why is the temperature constant during boiling?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">为什么沸腾时温度不变？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Energy separates particles into gas instead of making them move faster.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">能量用来把粒子分开成气体，而不是让它们跑得更快。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.c4", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which kinetic energy matters most for a phase change?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">对相变最重要的是哪种动能？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Translational — particles must move away from each other.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">平动动能——粒子必须彼此远离。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.c5", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Cooling curve flat parts for water?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的冷却曲线有哪两个水平段？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Condensation at 100 °C, freezing at 0 °C.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">100 °C 液化，0 °C 凝固。</span></div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "c5-heating-curve.p1", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">On a heating curve, a horizontal line means the ______ is changing while the temperature stays constant.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">加热曲线上，水平线表示______在变化，而温度不变。</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Melting and boiling happen here.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">熔化和沸腾发生在这里。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">phase (state)</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">相（状态）</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Horizontal = phase change, temperature constant.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水平线＝相变，温度不变。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.p2", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">At what temperature (°C) is the boiling segment (segment 4) for water?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的沸腾段（第 4 段）在多少摄氏度？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The first flat part is at 0 °C.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第一个水平段在 0 °C。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"\">100 °C</div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Segment 4 is boiling, at 100 °C for water.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 4 段是沸腾，水为 100 °C。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.p3", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">In which segment are both solid and liquid present?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">哪一段同时存在固体和液体？</span></div>", "opts": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "a": 1, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which flat part is at 0 °C?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">哪个水平段在 0 °C？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Segment 2 (melting, 0 °C)</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 2 段（熔化，0 °C）</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Segment 2 is melting: ice and liquid water together at 0 °C.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 2 段是熔化：0 °C 时冰和水共存。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.p4", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">In segment 3, is the temperature changing? If so, rising or falling?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 3 段温度在变吗？如果在变，是升还是降？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Is segment 3 diagonal or horizontal?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 3 段是斜线还是水平线？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Yes — rising from 0 °C to 100 °C (liquid water warming).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">在变——从 0 °C 升到 100 °C（液态水升温）。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Segment 3 is diagonal: liquid water warms from 0 °C to 100 °C, particles move faster.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 3 段是斜线：液态水从 0 °C 升到 100 °C，粒子运动加快。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.p5", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A sample of water is at 100 °C and both liquid and gas are present. Which segment number is it in?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">一份水处于 100 °C，液体和气体同时存在。它在第几段？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Count: 1 ice, 2 melting, 3 liquid, ...</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">数一数：1 冰，2 熔化，3 液体……</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">4</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 4 段</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Boiling is segment 4.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">沸腾是第 4 段。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.p6", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Why does the temperature stay constant while water boils, even though the burner is still on?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">为什么水沸腾时，即使火一直开着，温度也保持不变？</span></div>", "opts": ["<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The burner stops giving heat at 100 °C.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">到 100 °C 时，炉子就不再供热了。</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The heat makes the particles move faster, but the thermometer cannot read above 100 °C.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">热量让粒子跑得更快，只是温度计读不到 100 °C 以上。</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The water molecules are breaking into hydrogen and oxygen.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水分子正在分解成氢和氧。</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The heat is used to separate particles into the gas phase, not to make them move faster.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">热量用来把粒子分开、变成气体，而不是让它们跑得更快。</span></span>"], "a": 3, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Boiling is a physical change — the molecules stay <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">H</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord rlap\"><span class=\"inner\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:transparent;\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;color:transparent;\">X</span></span></span><span class=\"fix\"></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:-0.15em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">\u200b</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathrm\">O</span></span></span></span></span>.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">沸腾是物理变化——分子仍是 <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">H</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord rlap\"><span class=\"inner\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:transparent;\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;color:transparent;\">X</span></span></span><span class=\"fix\"></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:-0.15em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">\u200b</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathrm\">O</span></span></span></span></span>。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The heat separates particles into the gas phase instead of speeding them up.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">热量用于把粒子分开成气体，而不是让它们加速。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">During boiling, energy is used to pull particles away from their neighbours into the gas phase, not to increase their average speed, so the temperature stays at 100 °C.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">沸腾时，能量用来把粒子从邻近粒子中拉出、进入气相，而不是提高平均速度，所以温度保持在 100 °C。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.p7", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which kind of kinetic energy matters most for a phase change (rotational, vibrational or translational)?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">对相变最重要的是哪种动能（转动、振动还是平动）？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Spinning or shaking in place does not let a particle escape.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">原地转或原地抖都不能让粒子逃出去。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">translational</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">平动动能</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Only translational motion moves a particle from place to place, letting it break away from its neighbours.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">只有平动能让粒子从一处移到另一处，从而挣脱周围粒子。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c5-heating-curve.p8", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A student heats crushed ice from −15 °C at a steady rate and records: 0–2 min temperature rises to 0 °C; 2–8 min it stays at 0 °C; 8–16 min it rises to 100 °C. At minute 5: (a) what temperature does the thermometer show (°C)? (b) what is in the beaker? (c) what is the heat doing?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">某学生匀速加热 −15 °C 的碎冰，记录：0–2 分钟升到 0 °C；2–8 分钟保持 0 °C；8–16 分钟升到 100 °C。第 5 分钟时：(a) 温度计读数多少（°C）？(b) 烧杯里有什么？(c) 热量在做什么？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which time window contains minute 5?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 5 分钟落在哪个时间段？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">(a) 0 °C. (b) A mixture of ice and liquid water. (c) Breaking the attractions holding the ice particles together (melting), not raising the temperature.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">(a) 0 °C。(b) 冰和液态水的混合。(c) 打破冰中粒子之间的吸引（熔化），而不是升温。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Minute 5 is in the 2–8 min flat part at 0 °C → segment 2, melting.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">第 5 分钟在 2–8 分钟、0 °C 的水平段 → 第 2 段，熔化。</span></div>", "whys": null}], "v": 1, "key": "topic-c5-heating-curve"}